26,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems our history is mixed. Some water works held up, but surfacing and planting have been failures.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The ground is tricky. Clay and slippage are risks, and we can't easily close the main gate.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mio,,The costs are worrying. Planted areas are three times more expensive to maintain than hard surfaces.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Our internal staff is depleted, though we have some volunteers for habitat and sports.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"People use the center for commuting, and our drainage is struggling while the heat is rising.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, if planting is so expensive, we should be wary of any ""green"" plan that lacks a budget.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, if the center is a transit route, a complex layout might just get trampled.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! And @Asuka, if we have no staff, who is weeding the gardens?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,The volunteers are specific to habitat or sports. They won't just do general gardening.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,The drainage issues suggest we might need a plan that actually manages water rather than fighting it.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, that makes the wetland option interesting, provided the construction doesn't fail like the paving did.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Misaki,,But the earth-movers warned about slippage. A massive reshape for wetlands could be a nightmare.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Mio,,"A paved plaza would be the cheapest to maintain, but is it what the park needs?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"A sports terrace would utilize the existing sports volunteers, which solves the staffing gap.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,But the heat readings were high. A paved plaza or sports courts might just create a heat island.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,We need a balance of durability and utility.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Misaki,,And something that doesn't risk a construction collapse.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm leaning toward the plaza for the budget, but I'm listening.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I still think the sports terraces are the most sustainable for the current staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I think the wetland restoration addresses the drainage and heat, if we can build it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
